       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If so, please confirm it's intentional. I'd add a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max, intentional per attending\" so pharmacy and nursing don't treat it as an error.\n3. **Use a different regimen**, such as 10 mg of amlodipine plus a second agent like an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic, if the goal is more blood pressure control.\n\nOnce you tell me which one, I'll enter it."
      }
